# Obsidian vault (developer-io) — default workflow

Persistent project memory lives in the Obsidian vault **developer-io**.
Prefer the **Obsidian MCP** (`user-obsidian`) over reading vault files from disk.

Keep Obsidian open with this vault; Local REST API must be running.

## Transport (already configured)

Cursor connects to the plugin MCP at `https://127.0.0.1:27124/mcp/` (via `mcp-remote` in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`).

## Cold start (mandatory — every session)

Use Obsidian MCP tools, not the filesystem:

1. `vault_read` **only** `Projects/CRMC-Aims/_Card.md` (or `Projects/CourtSync/_Card.md`).
2. `vault_read` `Meta/Context-Loading-Protocol.md`, then **name** any additional notes for this task **before** reading them.
3. Feature-scoped work → `vault_read` **one** `Projects/<P>/Features/<slug>.md` — do **not** load full Architecture, Tasks, Sessions, or Components/Index unless the protocol says so.

Confirm ready after those reads.

## Cost / context rules

- Prefer `vault_get_document_map` + targeted `vault_read` / `vault_patch` — never dump full `Tasks.md` or `Sessions.md`.
- Write vault notes at **meaningful milestones or session end**, not every tiny prompt.
- `sessionStart` hook may inject sprint + last-session from `_Card` (cheap); do not re-read those notes unless updating them.

## During the session

| Need | MCP tool |
|------|----------|
| Structure / version | `vault_get_document_map` |
| Read a note | `vault_read` |
| List a folder | `vault_list` |
| Find notes | `search_simple` / `search_query` |
| Edit a heading / frontmatter | `vault_patch` |
| Append to a note | `vault_append` |
| Create / overwrite a note | `vault_write` |
| Open note in Obsidian UI | `open_file` |
| Tags | `tag_list` |

Use vault-relative paths with extension, e.g. `Projects/CRMC-Aims/Features/borrow-requests.md`.

## Do not

- Re-explore the repo when the card + feature note already name the hot paths
- Follow the old five-file bootstrap (Overview + Architecture + Conventions + Tasks + Sessions)
- Load `agents/*.examples.md` unless explicitly asked
- Use bare wikilinks like `[[Architecture]]` — use full paths under `Projects/CRMC-Aims/…`
- Bypass MCP to dump large vault trees into context
- Mandatory per-prompt Tasks write-back (too expensive)

## Session end

1. Update `_Card.md` last-session / sprint via `vault_patch` if it moved; sync Tasks checkboxes if you changed sprint state.
2. From vault root:

```bash
node Meta/scripts/vault-track.mjs session --project crmc-aims --write
node Meta/scripts/vault-track.mjs stale --project crmc-aims
```

Changelog only for pushed commits.

## Project overrides

When using specialized agents, also `vault_read` `Projects/CRMC-Aims/agent-overrides.md`.

## If MCP fails

If tools return `fetch failed`, open Obsidian with **developer-io** and confirm Local REST API is enabled. Fall back to reading the vault folder on disk only then.
